Two pieces of work planned at once, one done now: the user plans a README
section and a port change, and asks for the port change first. A later
session asked what is left names the README section, and not the port.

-- project/README.md --
# Acme

Run it with `make run`.
-- project/config.yaml --
port: 8080
-- prompt --
Plan two things as separate goals: add an "Install" section to README.md, and change the port in config.yaml to 9090. Do the port change now; the README can wait.
-- prompt-new --
What's left from what we planned?
-- check --
file config.yaml contains 9090
cmd ! grep -qi install README.md
answer last matches (?i)install
answer last matches (?i)readme
